msgctxt "areaDescription-comms"
msgid "City"
msgstr "City"

#: scripts/scenario_19_what_the_dickens.lua:839
msgctxt "areaDescription-comms"
msgid ""
"The City station represents one of the most developed stations in the area. "
"Correlating the station to olde Earth, this would be where the walled "
"medieval area of London would have been located"
msgstr "The City station represents one of the most developed stations in the area. Correlating the station to olde Earth, this would be where the walled medieval area of London would have been located"

#: scripts/scenario_19_what_the_dickens.lua:844
msgctxt "areaDescription-comms"
msgid "Change"
msgstr "Change"

#: scripts/scenario_19_what_the_dickens.lua:848
msgctxt "areaDescription-comms"
msgid ""
"Much of the area's financial business is handled at the station named "
"Change. The station name is an oblique reference to the Royal Exchange of "
"London"
msgstr "Much of the area's financial business is handled at the station named Change. The station name is an oblique reference to the Royal Exchange of London"

#: scripts/scenario_19_what_the_dickens.lua:854
msgctxt "areaDescription-comms"
msgid "Foundling"
msgstr "Foundling"

#: scripts/scenario_19_what_the_dickens.lua:859
msgctxt "areaDescription-comms"
msgid ""
"Foundling station specializes in medical research for children. The station "
"name honors Foundling Hospital in London, an orphanage established in 1739 "
"by Captain Thomas Coram, a retired seaman"
msgstr "Foundling station specialises in medical research for children. The station name honours Foundling Hospital in London, an orphanage established in 1739 by Captain Thomas Coram, a retired seaman"

#: scripts/scenario_19_what_the_dickens.lua:865
msgctxt "areaDescription-comms"
msgid "Thames"
msgstr "Thames"

#: scripts/scenario_19_what_the_dickens.lua:869
msgctxt "areaDescription-comms"
msgid ""
"The zone running through this area colored blue is named Thames after the "
"river Thames in London of olde Earth. Ships should avoid entering this "
"zoneexcept by bridges designated due to the adverse effects it has on ship "
"systems. This is why navigation systems automatically show this region for "
"all ships in the area."
msgstr "The zone running through this area coloured blue is named Thames after the river Thames in London of olde Earth. Ships should avoid entering this zoneexcept by bridges designated due to the adverse effects it has on ship systems. This is why navigation systems automatically show this region for all ships in the area."

#: scripts/scenario_19_what_the_dickens.lua:874
msgctxt "areaDescription-comms"
msgid "Covent"
msgstr "Covent"

#: scripts/scenario_19_what_the_dickens.lua:878
msgctxt "areaDescription-comms"
msgid ""
"Most of the area's food supply comes from station Covent. It specializes in "
"hydroponics. THe station derives its name from Covent Garden from olde Earth "
"London where fruits, vegetables and flowers were bought and sold"
msgstr "Most of the area's food supply comes from station Covent. It specialises in hydroponics. THe station derives its name from Covent Garden from olde Earth London where fruits, vegetables and flowers were bought and sold"

#: scripts/scenario_19_what_the_dickens.lua:883
